<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław Odonic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1190–1239</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław Odonic was a Piast Duke of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> who fought his uncle Władysław Spindleshanks for the duchy and won it after 1229. He relied on the support of the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a>, granting the church wide privileges, and his sons Przemysł I and Bolesław the Pious consolidated Greater Poland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-odonic.jpg" alt="Władysław Odonic" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franciszek Piekosiński · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wladyslaw_Odonic_seal_1231_(16839134).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
